G` lookup, then the key itself as fallback (no error).\n- Interpolation: Calls `interpolate()` with params; undefined params remain as `{name}`.\n- Example: `t('promotionQueue.columns.status')` → `\"Status\"`; `t('memoryInbox.pagination.showing', {start: 1, end: 10, total: 100})` → `\"Showing 1-10 of 100\"`.\n\n**i18n.has(key)** — returns boolean; checks catalog and fallback.\n\n**No ICU support.** Pluralization would require client-side branching (e.g., `count === 1 ? singular : plural`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Duplicates\n\nScanning for string-value duplicates across namespaces:\n- `\"Refresh\"`, `\"Retry\"`, `\"Loading\"`, `\"Error\"`, etc. appear in multiple namespaces (by design for UI reuse).\n- **Intentional:** `reviewPanel.loading` / `memoryInbox.loadingHint` / `staleView.loadingHint` / `evidenceInspector.reverifyLoading` / `consolidationQueueView.actions.retrying` / `indexingHealthView.actions.refreshing` are semantically distinct scopes (different views).\n- No string value appears in two keys with identical intent; all duplicates are contextual variants."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f5c8929-5870-493f-9d77-6b17226dfdaa","uuid":"8a63f763-27ec-431e-8230-18eb27dcc68f","timestamp":"2026-05-17T18:18:10.669Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the i18n catalog at /home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/review/i18n/en.json and the i18n helper at /home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/review/i18n/index.ts.\n\nI need a report covering:\n\n1. Top-level namespaces present in the JSON catalog. The expected ones per the R78 review task are: panel, statusBadge, memoryInbox, promotionQueue, contradictionQueue, proposalDialog, staleView, evidenceInspector, eventTraceView, retrievalExplanationView, consolidationQueueView, indexingHealthView, workspaceGraphHealthView. State which are present and which are missing.\n\n2. For EACH namespace, count keys and list the top-level keys (titles, columns, actions, empty, error, etc.). Spot-check wheth