{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NtDyqaaGS9LUZAbVA9SvGe","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now let me create a comprehensive summary based on my findings:\n\n## Audit Report: Review Components (StatusBadge & Modal Patterns)\n\n### 1. StatusBadge Centralization Audit\n\n**File:** `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/review/components/StatusBadge.ts` (65 lines total)\n\n**Status Families Supported:** 18 statuses mapped in `STATUS_PRESENTATION` record (lines 31-49):\n- Verification statuses (8 required by R78): `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated` ✓\n- Proposal statuses: `pending`, `applied`, `rejected`, `reverted`, `proposed`\n- Job/process statuses: `queued`, `running`, `failed`, `dropped`\n\n**Coverage:** All 8 R78 verification statuses are present and properly mapped.\n\n**Exported Functions:**\n- `renderStatusBadge(status: VerificationStatus | string, i18n: ReviewI18nLike): string` (line 52)\n  - Returns escaped HTML span with semantic CSS class and i18n label\n  - Fallback for unknown statuses: `status-badge--muted` with `reviewPanel.statusUnknown` label\n\n**Color/Label Mapping Strategy:** Token-driven via semantic CSS classes, not hardcoded hex colors:\n- Classes: `status-badge--success`, `status-badge--warning`, `status-badge--danger`, `status-badge--info`, `status-badge--muted`\n- Colors resolved at style-time via `reviewPanelHtml.ts` CSS variables (`--vscode-*` theme tokens)\n- Labels keyed via i18n: `reviewStatus.*` namespace\n\n**Duplicate Mapping Search Results:** No alternate status-to-color/label mappings found elsewhere in `extension/src/review/`. All references respect the single source of truth in StatusBadge.ts. One secondary pattern exists in `eventTraceView.ts:364-374` for event kind badges (not verification status), which correctly uses distinct CSS classes (`status-badge--error`, `status-badge--info`, `status-badge--success`, `status-badge--neutral`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Modal Pattern Audit\n\n**ProposalDialog** (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/review/components/ProposalDialog.ts`):\n- **Native `<dialog>` element:** Yes (line 33, created with `document.createElement('dialog')`)\n- **Backdrop:** Yes, defined in CSS (reviewPanelHtml.ts line 1822: `.proposal-dialog::backdrop { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45); }`)\n- **Escape handling:** Native to `<dialog>` element (Escape key closes automatically via `dialog.close()`)\n- **Focus management:** Yes (lines 189-195):\n  - If mode is 'reject': focus on reason input\n  - If typed confirm required OR mode is 'accept': focus on confirm input\n  - Default: focus on accept button\n- **Type-to-confirm for destructive actions:** Yes (lines 124-138):\n  - Required for repo/user/organization scope (high-scope changes)\n  - Confirm token generated from `proposedClass` with alphanumerics only (line 92, 361-362)\n  - Accept button disabled until typed confirm matches (line 138: `confirmInput.value.trim() !== confirmToken`)\n  - Reject action requires reason textarea input (line 133: `reasonInput.value.trim().length === 0` disables button)\n\n**EventTraceView payload dialog** (`eventTraceView.ts:163-178`):\n- **Purpose:** Display event payload JSON in a modal for inspection/copying\n- **Native `<dialog>` element:** Yes (line 163: `<dialog id=\"payload-${...}\" class=\"payload-dialog\">`)\n- **Open/Close:** \n  - Opens via `data-local-command=\"open-dialog\"` button trigger (line 150)\n  - Closes via `data-local-command=\"close-dialog\"` button or native Escape (line 173)\n  - Handled by review panel's local command dispatcher (reviewPanelHtml.ts lines 2255-2266)\n\n**VSCode API Prompts** (used for pick/input flows):\n- `vscode.window.showQuickPick()` — used 5 times in reviewPanel.ts (lines 526, 716, 738, 1209, 1292, 1316, 2527) for interactive selection\n- `vscode.window.showInformationMessage()` — used 4 times (lines 352, 767, 794, 1268) with `{ modal: true }` option (line 1255)\n- **Compliance:** VSCode APIs use native OS dialogs, avoiding `window.confirm/prompt/alert` — conforming to UI spec §7\n\n**Interactive Prompting Sites:**\n- Memory promotion flow (reviewPanel.ts:716) — QuickPick for scope selection\n- Event trace filtering (reviewPanel.ts:526, 738, 1209, 1292, 1316) — QuickPick for kinds/actors/scope\n- Consolidation retry confirmation (reviewPanel.ts:1253-1255) — showInformationMessage with modal flag\n- Copy payload feedback (reviewPanel.ts:1382) — showInformationMessage\n\n**No window.confirm/prompt/alert found** in review tree. All modals follow native dialog or VSCode API patterns.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nStatusBadge is properly centralized with complete R78 coverage and semantic (not hardcoded) styling. ProposalDialog follows best practices with native `<dialog>`, backdrop, focus management, Escape handling, and type-to-confirm for high-scope destructive actions. All interactive prompts use native or VSCode APIs, avoiding deprecated browser dialogs."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f5c8929-5870-493f-9d77-6b17226dfdaa","uuid":"8c3ef10e-80d7-4dbc-af54-df453bc72688","timestamp":"2026-05-17T18:18:42.946Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Two audits in /home/pete/cadres/lattice/extension/src/review/:\n\n1. **StatusBadge centralization.** Read extension/src/review/components/StatusBadge.ts and report:\n   - All status families/labels it supports (verification, proposal, job, decision, etc.)\n   - Whether it covers all 8 verification statuses required by R78: verified, unverified, in_review, stale, contradicted, superseded, expired, invalidated\n   - The exported function(s) and their signatures\n   - Whether color/label mapping is hard-coded or token-driven (semantic CSS vars vs hex colors)\n   - The full file is only ~65 lines so a complete walkthrough is feasible.\n\n   Then grep the entire extension/src/review/ tree (excluding StatusBadge.ts itse